{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001","f011","f015"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s01; BRANCH=terminator-write-off-by-one; New mechanism branch revealed by f015 and flagged unresolved in s01 by f011: the seed fix primitive (an explicit NUL terminator slot) misapplied so the terminator write itself lands out of bounds - a length clamp without -1 (len = min_t(size_t, count, sizeof(buf)) or min(count, sizeof(buf)), or accepting count == sizeof(buf)) followed by buf[len] = 0 where len can equal the buffer or allocation size, producing a 1-byte OOB write; this is the inverse consequence of the seed's missing-terminator OOB read under the same terminator-slot accounting root cause. Search only snapshots/s01 and no other snapshot. First resolve the unresolved candidate drivers/edac/versal_edac.c inject_data_ue_store (char buf[6], clamp, then buf[len] = 0) with line-level bound analysis, and examine drivers/edac/zynqmp_edac.c inject_ue_write for the identical pattern; then sweep every write interface in snapshots/s01 (debugfs .write, sysfs/configfs ->store with own copy_from_user, proc .proc_write, scsi host ->write_info callbacks, char-device and ioctl writers, module_param handlers) for clamp-then-terminate sites where the terminator index can reach sizeof(buf) or the allocation size, including PAGE_SIZE-allocated pages. Reject with concrete evidence where count > sizeof(buf)-1 is rejected before the copy (reference: drivers/iio/industrialio-core.c, drivers/platform/x86/intel/pmc/core.c) or the allocation is len+1 (reference: mm/vmscan.c kvmalloc(len+1)). Record file:line, clamp expression, buffer size, terminator index, and bound analysis; a negative evidence-backed result is valid. Save a structured JSON artifact for snapshot s01 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001","f015"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s02; BRANCH=terminator-write-off-by-one; New mechanism branch first verified in this snapshot by f015 with an ASan harness: a length clamp without -1 (len = min_t(size_t, count, sizeof(buf))) followed by a terminator write buf[len] = 0 where len can equal the buffer size, a 1-byte OOB write that is the seed fix primitive misapplied (inverse of the seed's missing-terminator OOB read, same terminator-slot accounting root cause). Search only snapshots/s02 and no other snapshot. The already-reported instances drivers/edac/versal_edac.c inject_data_ue_store and drivers/edac/zynqmp_edac.c inject_ue_write (char buf[6], buf[6] = 0 when count >= 6) must be cited as known, not re-reported; instead enumerate every OTHER write handler in snapshots/s02 (proc .proc_write, scsi host ->write_info callbacks such as wd33c93/imm/ppa, debugfs .write with direct copy_from_user or simple_write_to_buffer, char-device and ioctl writers, sysfs/configfs stores doing their own copy) where a clamp or a count == sizeof(buf) acceptance lets the terminator index reach the buffer or allocation size, including the PAGE_SIZE proc page boundary case in drivers/scsi/scsi_proc.c ->write_info callers. Reject with concrete evidence where count > sizeof(buf)-1 is enforced before the terminator write or the allocation is len+1. Record file:line, clamp expression, buffer size, terminator index, and bound analysis; a negative evidence-backed result is valid. Save a structured JSON artifact for snapshot s02 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001","f005","f015"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s03; BRANCH=terminator-write-off-by-one; New mechanism branch (seed fix primitive misapplied: a length clamp without -1 followed by a terminator write buf[len] = 0 at an index that can equal the buffer or allocation size - a 1-byte OOB write, the inverse of the seed's missing-terminator OOB read under the same terminator-slot accounting root cause). Search only snapshots/s03 and no other snapshot. Resolve two recorded contradictions with line-level evidence: (1) f005 classified drivers/edac/versal_edac.c inject_data_ue_store (char buf[6], len = min_t(count, sizeof(buf)), then buf[len] = 0) as safe/terminated while f015 verified the byte-identical pattern as a 1-byte stack OOB write - read the actual code in this snapshot and settle it; (2) f005 finding 1 claims wd33c93.c buf[len] = 0 can write one byte past a PAGE_SIZE page when count == PAGE_SIZE while f005/f016 elsewhere record PROC_BLOCK_SIZE as 3*1024 - verify the real PROC_BLOCK_SIZE in drivers/scsi/scsi_proc.c and the wd33c93/imm/ppa ->write_info terminator bounds. Then examine drivers/edac/zynqmp_edac.c inject_ue_write and sweep every other write interface in snapshots/s03 (debugfs .write, proc .proc_write, char-device/ioctl writers, sysfs/configfs stores with own copy_from_user, module_param handlers) for clamp-then-terminate off-by-one sites. Reject with concrete evidence where count > sizeof(buf)-1 is enforced or the allocation is len+1. Record file:line, clamp, buffer size, terminator index, bound analysis; a negative evidence-backed result is valid. Save a structured JSON artifact for snapshot s03 only."}
{"event":"intent","sources":["origin","f001","f008","f015"],"description":"SNAPSHOT=s04; BRANCH=terminator-write-off-by-one; New mechanism branch (seed fix primitive misapplied: a length clamp without -1 followed by a terminator write buf[len] = 0 where the index can equal the buffer or allocation size - a 1-byte OOB write, the inverse of the seed's missing-terminator OOB read under the same terminator-slot accounting root cause). Search only snapshots/s04 and no other snapshot. Resolve the recorded contradiction: f008 classified drivers/edac/versal_edac.c inject_data_ue_store (char buf[6], len = min_t(size_t, count, sizeof(buf)), then buf[len] = 0) as safe, reasoning that an index bounded by sizeof(buf) = 6 stays in bounds, which conflicts with f015's ASan-verified analysis of the identical pattern (buf[6] on char buf[6] is one byte past the array) - re-read the code in this snapshot line-by-line and settle safe versus 1-byte stack OOB write. Examine drivers/edac/zynqmp_edac.c inject_ue_write for the same pattern, then sweep every write interface in snapshots/s04 (debugfs .write, proc .proc_write, scsi host ->write_info callbacks, char-device and ioctl writers, sysfs/configfs stores with own copy_from_user, module_param handlers) for clamp-then-terminate sites where the terminator index can reach the destination size, including PAGE_SIZE-allocated buffers. Reject with concrete evidence where count > sizeof(buf)-1 is rejected before the terminator write or the allocation is len+1. Record file:line, clamp expression, buffer size, terminator index, and bound analysis; a negative evidence-backed result is valid. Save a structured JSON artifact for snapshot s04 only."}
